/******************************************
Created by: Mason Newman
Date: January 2026

Originally written for Raspberry Pi PICO 2W (RP2350)

This sketch was created to test drawing bitmaps to TFT LCD. The bitmaps include backgrounds as well as dynamic sprites. 
The goal is to display these sprites in a way that reduces flicker and keeps load on MCU low. 
The first display used was the 1.44" TFT using a ST7735 driver.
The first step was to display a static background. 
The second step was to initiate partial redraws on dynamic sprites to indicate selections based on button inputs.
The third step was to add multiple dynamic sprites controlled by button inputs.
The fourht step was to create a smooth continous animation that does not block button reads.
The fifth step was to add in UART listening functioanlity from another MCU.
The sixth step will be to display a dynamic value based on received UART value.

This is the port for the larger TFT using a RA8875 driver. 
To do this the bitmap sizes and locations need to be scaled back up to the original commented values. 
The larger bitmaps then need to be converted to C arrays and added into the code under the correct definitions. 
Finally, the libraries need to be switched.

******************************************/

